 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "This repo is a Flask-like framework (`tessel`) with renamed APIs.\n\n**How `request`, `session` and `g` get into templates**\n- `render_template`, `render_template_string`, `stream_template` and `stream_template_string` in `src/tessel/templating.py` all go through `_render` or `_stream`. Both call `app.fill_template_scope(ctx, context)`.\n- `fill_template_scope` is in `src/tessel/app.py:588`. It runs every registered context injector and merges the results into the context. Values you pass to `render_template` take precedence over injector values.\n- The default injector is `_base_template_vars()` (`src/tessel/templating.py:21`). It is pre-registered under the `None` key in `template_ctx_injectors` (`src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:182-184`).\n- `_base_template_vars()` returns `g` and, when a request exists, `request`. It replaces those proxies with the real objects.\n- `session` isn't injected by that function. The code comment says the proxy can't be replaced. It comes from the `session` proxy in `src/tessel/globals.py:61`.\n- I didn't find where `session` becomes a Jinja global. I only read the injector path, so I can't confirm that part.\n\n**Adding your own variables**\n- Use the `@ctx_injector` decorator, defined in `src/tessel/sansio/scaffold.py:550`. Your function takes no arguments and returns a dict.\n  - On the app, it applies to every template.\n  - On a bundle, it applies only to templates rendered from that bundle's views.\n- For a bundle-level function that affects every template, use `@bundle.app_ctx_injector` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:644`).",
